@@s027 The chain of reductions
@@s028 From 3-SAT to everything else (the scheme of the slides)
@@s029 The easy look-alikes
@@s030 Every hard problem has a <b>twin</b> that looks the same but is solved in polynomial time. What changes is a detail: a cycle that passes through every <i>node</i> is hard, a cycle that passes through every <i>edge</i> is easy.
